    "metadata": {
      "source": "synthetic-voice-transport",
      "split": "public-barge-in",
      "family": "bargein_cut_reference_is_repeated",
      "note": "The line is full-duplex, so the caller cutting in at the second word means the reference number never reached them — while the model's own history still holds the whole sentence, because nothing tells it where it was cut. The milestone therefore scores `against: \"heard\"`: 'the caller was told the reference' is a claim about the caller, not about what was emitted. The model is never asked to know it was interrupted, only to answer the question it is then asked."
    }
